{"defs":{},"properties":[{"path":["schema:additionalType"],"id":"http://schema.org/additionalType","description":"Domain-specific type classifications for this place (e.g. facility type,laboratory classification, feature type).","required":true,"schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent","bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.xasProperties.xasFacility"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/additionalType"},{"path":["schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"A place name for the location, either as a string or a DefinedTerm from a gazetteer.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","description":"Formal identifier for this place (e.g. ROR identifier for a facility).","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:alternateName"],"id":"http://schema.org/alternateName","description":"Alternate or abbreviated name(s) for this place.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/alternateName"},{"path":["schema:geo"],"id":"http://schema.org/geo","description":"Either a bounding box or a point location.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/geo"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf"],"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"anyOf"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","0"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","0","schema:latitude"],"id":"http://schema.org/latitude","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/latitude"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","0","schema:longitude"],"id":"http://schema.org/longitude","required":true,"schema_type":"number","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/longitude"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","1"],"title":"b","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","1","schema:box"],"id":"http://schema.org/box","description":"A GeoShape box defines an area on the surface of the earth defined by point locations of the southwest corner and northeast corner of the rectangle in latitude-longitude coordinates. A space should be used to separate the latitude and longitude values. The two corner coordinate points are separated by a space. 'East longitude' means positive longitude values are east of the prime (Greenwich) meridian.","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/box"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","2"],"title":"c","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:geo","_anyOf","2","schema:line"],"id":"http://schema.org/line","description":"A GeoShape box defines a curvilinear geometry as a string of latitude-longitude coordinates. A space should be used to separate the latitude and longitude values. The coordinate point pairs are also separated by a space. 'East longitude' means positive longitude values are east of the prime (Greenwich) meridian. e.g. '39.33 120.77 40.44 123.96 41.00 121.34' ","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/line"},{"path":["geosparql:hasGeometry"],"description":"Optional geographic extent using wkt geometry, see Ocean InfoHub (https://book.oceaninfohub.org/thematics/spatial/README.html#simple-geosparql-wkt). Other geometry schemes might be specified in a specific domain profile, e.g. for atmospheric, subsurface data, or local coordinate systems. NOTE that the location specified here should be the same as the schema.org point or contained within the specified bounding box.","schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["geosparql:hasGeometry","geosparql:asWKT"],"required":true,"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["geosparql:hasGeometry","geosparql:crs"],"schema_type":"object","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.spatialExtent"]},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty"],"id":"http://schema.org/additionalProperty","description":"Facility-scope properties that are not places, e.g. storage-ring energy or current. Not offered by the core block, which describes a location rather than an operating machine.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.xasProperties.xasFacility"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/additionalProperty"},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty","schema:propertyID"],"id":"http://schema.org/propertyID","description":"identifier or name for the property concept quantified by the values in this variable slot. Multiple values can specify the property at different levels of granularity.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.additionalProperty"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/propertyID"},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","required":true,"schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.additionalProperty"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.additionalProperty"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty","schema:unitCode"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitCode","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.additionalProperty"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitCode"},{"path":["schema:additionalProperty","schema:unitText"],"id":"http://schema.org/unitText","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.additionalProperty"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/unitText"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2"],"title":"a","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"keyword":"branch"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:narrower"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower","description":"Narrower (child) concepts in the hierarchy. Items are inline concept objects or @id references.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrower"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:broader"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader","description":"Broader (parent) concepts in the hierarchy. Items are inline concept objects or @id references.","schema_type":"array","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:topConceptOf"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf","description":"Concept scheme(s) for which this is a top concept.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#topConceptOf"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:inScheme"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme","description":"Concept scheme(s) this concept belongs to.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:editorialNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote","description":"Note for editors and maintainers.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:changeNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote","description":"Note documenting a change.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:historyNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote","description":"Note about past state or use.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:note"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note","description":"General note about this concept.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:scopeNote"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote","description":"Note clarifying meaning and/or intended use.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:definition"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition","description":"Formal explanation of the meaning of this concept.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:notation"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation","description":"Classification code for this concept within a scheme (a single notation string, consistent with CdifCodelistConcept).","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","2","skos:prefLabel"],"id":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel","description":"Preferred lexical label for this concept. A single string, a single language-tagged value, or an array of language-tagged values. Each language should appear at most once.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:termCode"],"id":"http://schema.org/termCode","description":"A representative code for this keyword in the controlled vocabulary. Analogous to skos:Notation","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/termCode"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:inDefinedTermSet"],"id":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet","description":"The controlled vocabulary responsible for this keyword, as EITHER a plain URI string identifying the vocabulary, OR an object reference ({\"@id\": \"<uri>\"}) to a vocabulary defined elsewhere in the document. Both forms are already in use across CDIF profiles and downstream ADA building blocks; permitting only the string form made the object form - the natural JSON-LD spelling of a reference - invalid, while this class's own union-type policy above explicitly anticipates both.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:propertyID"],"id":"http://schema.org/propertyID","description":"In this context for the schema:PropertyValue, this field is an identifier for the identifier schema, e.g. DOI, ARK.  Get values from https://registry.identifiers.org/registry/ for interoperability. URI-shape values MUST be serialized as JSON-LD IRI references ({\"@id\":\"...\"}) so they participate in RDF entailment; free-label strings remain valid as strings.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/propertyID"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","description":"the identifier string. E.g. 10.5066/F7VX0DMQ","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","description":"web-resolveable string for the identifier; host name part is location of a resolver that will return some representation for the given identifier value. E.g. https://doi.org/10.5066/F7VX0DMQ ","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["schema:additionalType","_anyOf","1","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"text label for the term that is useful to human user","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"}]}